## **Part II: Sitting & Floor Postures**

### **1. Core & Strength**
* **Forward Bend (Sitting):** Reach for feet. [cite: 1]
* **Reverse Plank:** Lift hips with hands behind you. [cite: 1]
* **Side Plank:** Perform on the right side, then the left. [cite: 1]
* **Half Plank:** Hold for **10 breaths**. [cite: 1]

### **2. Hip Openers**
* **Pigeon Pose (Right):** Right leg in front, shin perpendicular to the body. Relax down on top of it. [cite: 1]
    * **Duration:** 12 breaths. [cite: 1]
* **Downward Dog:** Transition for **3 breaths**. [cite: 1]
* **Pigeon Pose (Left):** Left leg in front, shin perpendicular to the body. Relax down on top of it. [cite: 1]
    * **Duration:** 12 breaths. [cite: 1]

### **3. Seated Twists & ABS**
* **Simple Twist:** Right side, then left side. [cite: 1]
* **ABS (Core Lifts):** Perform **5 sets of 5 breaths**. Cross your legs and lift your butt off the floor between each set. [cite: 1]

### **4. Supine (Lying Down) Sequence**
* **Reclined Big Toe Hold (Right):** Extend the heel up, move it to the side (keep left hip grounded), then bend the knee and cross the body (keep right shoulder grounded). [cite: 1]
* **Reclined Big Toe Hold (Left):** Extend the heel up, move it to the side (keep right hip grounded), then bend the knee and cross the body (keep left shoulder grounded). [cite: 1]
* **Backbends:** Wheel or Camel pose. [cite: 1]
    * **Repetitions:** 3 sets of 10 breaths each. [cite: 1]
    * **Rest:** 3-breath break between each set. [cite: 1]
* **Counter Postures:** Hug the knees to the chest, then hold the feet for **Happy Baby**. [cite: 1]
* **Closing Folds:** Seated Forward Bend, then roll back into **Plough**. [cite: 1]

### **5. Finishing Posture**
* **Inversion:** Straighten up into **Shoulder Stand** or practice **Headstand**. [cite: 1]
* **Rest:** REST in Shavasana. [cite: 1]

