## **Part III: Pranayam & Meditation**

### **1. Bandhas (Internal Locks)**
* **Vajroli/Moolabandha/Ashwini:** Inhale and constrict (urethra, pelvic floor, or anus respectively), then relax on exhale. [cite: 1]
* **Hold:** Engage Moolabandha and hold for **10 breaths**. [cite: 1]

### **2. Breathwork (Pranayam)**
* **Anulom-Vilom (Alternate Nostril):** 10 sets. [cite: 1]
    * Inhale Left (2s) -> Hold (4s) -> Exhale Right -> Hold (4s). [cite: 1]
    * Inhale Right -> Hold (4s) -> Exhale Left. [cite: 1]
* **Breath of Fire:** **30 repetitions for 3 sets**. Take 3 long breaths between sets. [cite: 1]
* **Belly Rolling:** On a complete exhale, roll the belly clockwise (10 times) and counter-clockwise (10 times). [cite: 1]
* **Cathartic Breaths:**
    * **Crying Breath:** Inhale deep, exhale in short breaths with the "feeling of crying" while shaking the whole body (**10 breaths**). [cite: 1]
    * **Laughter Breath:** Inhale deep, exhale in short breaths with the "feeling of laughter" while shaking the whole body (**10 breaths**). [cite: 1]
* **Bellows Breath:** Inhale and extend arms; exhale and drive elbows hard against ribs. **50 times for 3 sets**. Take 3 long breaths between sets. [cite: 1]

### **3. Movement & Awareness**
* **Dancing Twists:** Perform with hands low, chest high, and above the head, plus circles forward and back. [cite: 1]
    * **Duration:** 10 breaths each. [cite: 1]
* **Body Scan Awareness:** Focus on the mouth, nose, center of the forehead, and top of the head. [cite: 1]
    * **Duration:** 10 breaths. [cite: 1]
    * **Scan:** Move from the top of the head to the base of the spine. [cite: 1]

**Final Step:** Meditate or done! [cite: 1]

